# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust. NEVER commit real secrets.

# Active use-case (folder under usecases/).
AGENT_USECASE=tienda

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tier topology (ADR-011)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resident memory, not token cost, is the binding constraint on a workstation.
# Tier 0 is small, hot and grammar-constrained, so it stays local; higher tiers
# are large and called rarely, so they go remote and cost 0 GB.
#
# Leave every AGENT_TIER{1,2,3}_* variable unset for the LOCAL-ONLY profile:
# the higher tiers are dropped at config load and all escalation resolves to
# Tier 0. Nothing else needs editing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Tier 0: local router/guardrail (default profile) ---
# Host directory containing your GGUF models (mounted read-only into llama.cpp).
MODELS_DIR=/home/youruser/ml-models
# Tier-0 router model filename inside MODELS_DIR.
E4B_MODEL=gemma-4-E4B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf
# Override only to move Tier 0 off the default llama.cpp endpoint.
# AGENT_TIER0_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8091/v1/chat/completions
# AGENT_TIER0_KIND=local

# --- Tiers 1-3: remote providers (HYBRID profile) ---
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint. Set URL + MODEL + API_KEY
# for each tier you want to enable; unset tiers collapse to the tier below.
# The model id is REQUIRED for a remote tier — providers reject an unset model,
# so config load fails fast rather than at the first request.
#
# AGENT_TIER1_URL=https://<provider-host>/v1/chat/completions
# AGENT_TIER1_MODEL=<provider-model-id>
# AGENT_TIER1_API_KEY=
#
# AGENT_TIER2_URL=https://<provider-host>/v1/chat/completions
# AGENT_TIER2_MODEL=<provider-model-id>
# AGENT_TIER2_API_KEY=
#
# AGENT_TIER3_URL=https://<provider-host>/v1/chat/completions
# AGENT_TIER3_MODEL=<provider-model-id>
# AGENT_TIER3_API_KEY=

# --- ALL-REMOTE profile (CI, no GGUF available) ---
# Point Tier 0 at a remote endpoint too. Routing then falls back from GBNF to
# `response_format: json_object` — syntactically constrained but NOT schema
# constrained, so this profile is not the quality-gated path (ADR-011).
# AGENT_TIER0_URL=https://<provider-host>/v1/chat/completions
# AGENT_TIER0_KIND=remote
# AGENT_TIER0_MODEL=<provider-model-id>
# AGENT_TIER0_API_KEY_ENV=AGENT_TIER0_API_KEY
# AGENT_TIER0_API_KEY=
